  <Widget no="2" caption="check yourself" widget="quiz" config={raceQuizCfg} />
  <p>
    <strong>What to notice:</strong> the questions retrace the page's four panels in
    evidence form — the construction claim, the audit study, hypodescent as a legal
    instrument, and Cooley's looking-glass self. Watch how each correct answer turns on
    the same move: separating origin from effect, and mechanism from intention. If the
    "one-drop rule" item tempts a biological answer, reread "Race as a construction that
    works": no biology can produce an "any amount counts" rule.
  </p>
